CORE
main.c
--report-unreachable-properties
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 12 dead branch: UNREACHABLE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line 19 reachable and true: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
A property that symex never reached is reported as UNREACHABLE rather than
SUCCESS, so that it cannot be mistaken for a property that was checked. A
reachable property is unaffected. Without the option both are SUCCESS, which
is the historical behaviour and is covered by the sibling test.
